      ⍝ Regression ----------------------------------
      ⍝
      (2 2⍴⍳4)[1;⍬]

      ⍴(2 2⍴⍳4)[1;⍬]
0

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(f)): indexed ASSIGNMENT through an empty
      ⍝ index used to silently no-op regardless of B, instead of
      ⍝ requiring B to conform (0 elements) just like a non-empty index
      ⍝ already does (Z[1;1 2]←1 2 3, below, was already correctly
      ⍝ LENGTH ERROR).
      ⍝
      Z←2 2⍴1
      Z[1;⍬]←1 2
LENGTH ERROR+
      Z[1;⍬]←1 2
      ^     ^

      )MORE
A[B]←C: an index is empty, so the selected area is empty, but C has 2 element(s) (expecting 0)
      )SIC

      ⍝ control: a conforming (empty) B through an empty index is a
      ⍝ genuine no-op
      ⍝
      Z[1;⍬]←⍬
      Z
1 1
1 1

      ⍝ control: this was already correctly rejected before the fix
      ⍝
      Z[1;1 2]←1 2 3
LENGTH ERROR+
      Z[1;1 2]←1 2 3
      ^       ^

      )SIC
      )ERASE Z

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(s)): the single-axis form of indexed
      ⍝ assignment (A[B]←C, no semicolons) only checked C's ELEMENT
      ⍝ COUNT against the index's, never that C was actually a vector,
      ⍝ so a wrongly-shaped C whose element count happened to match
      ⍝ (e.g. a 2 1 matrix for a 2-element index) silently succeeded
      ⍝ instead of RANK ERROR.
      ⍝
      W←10 20 30 40
      W[1 2]←2 1⍴1 2
RANK ERROR+
      W[1 2]←2 1⍴1 2
      ^     ^

      )MORE
A[B]←C: expecting ⍴C to be ⍴B (2); ⍴C is 2 1
      )SIC

      ⍝ control: a proper vector and a 1-element (scalar-extended) C
      ⍝ are unaffected
      ⍝
      W[1 2]←5 6
      W
5 6 30 40

      W[1 2]←,99
      W
99 99 30 40

      )ERASE W

